WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.870
Billie Elliot, by Melvin Burgess, based on a motion picture screenplay written by Lee

00:10.920 --> 00:00:12.390
Hall.

00:12.440 --> 00:00:18.030
Copyright 2005, Universal Studios Licensing, LLLP.

00:18.080 --> 00:00:24.630
Adapted by Jackie Bloosey.

00:24.680 --> 00:00:26.190
Chapter 1

00:26.240 --> 00:28.320
Billie, I love to boogie.

00:30.160 --> 00:00:32.950
I hate my brother.

00:33.000 --> 00:00:37.470
He's stupid, but he has got some good music.

00:37.520 --> 00:00:41.230
I listen to his music when he's out at work with my dad.

00:41.280 --> 00:00:46.030
Well, they're not at work, not now.

00:46.080 --> 00:00:48.310
They're on strike.

00:48.360 --> 00:00:52.350
But they still go to the mine every day.

00:52.400 --> 00:00:55.190
Nan loves the music too.

00:55.240 --> 00:00:57.750
Tony and Dad leave in the morning.

00:57.800 --> 00:01:03.910
When the music goes on, I make breakfast for us, and we both dance.

01:03.960 --> 00:01:06.510
I can hear her in her bedroom.

01:06.560 --> 00:01:09.870
She tries to dance, but she can't walk very well now.

01:09.920 --> 00:01:13.350
Well, she is 80.

01:13.400 --> 00:01:17.070
This morning, I made the eggs and danced to her bedroom.

01:17.120 --> 00:01:20.870
Hey, Nan, breakfast, I called.

01:20.920 --> 00:01:27.150
I open the door with my foot and, oh no, not again.

01:27.200 --> 00:01:29.470
Her bed was empty.

01:29.520 --> 00:01:33.430
I put the eggs on the kitchen table and ran out of the house.

01:33.480 --> 00:01:36.030
But where was she?

01:36.080 --> 00:01:37.950
She does this a lot.

01:38.000 --> 00:01:40.030
She forgets things.

01:40.080 --> 00:01:42.790
She forgets her name.

01:42.840 --> 00:01:44.950
I looked up the street.

01:45.000 --> 00:01:45.950
Nan?

01:46.000 --> 00:01:47.430
Nan?

01:47.480 --> 00:01:49.270
Which way?

01:49.320 --> 00:01:50.910
Then I had an idea.

01:50.960 --> 00:01:54.270
I ran to the end of the street and up to some trees.

01:54.320 --> 00:01:56.550
There she was.

01:56.600 --> 00:01:58.310
She often goes there.

01:58.360 --> 00:02:00.270
Why?

02:00.320 --> 00:02:02.150
Who knows?

02:02.200 --> 00:02:05.350
Maybe she played there when she was little.

02:05.400 --> 00:02:06.550
She looked frightened.

02:06.600 --> 00:02:09.470
Who are you?

02:09.520 --> 00:02:11.670
She said.

02:11.720 --> 00:02:14.990
It's me, Nan, Billy.

02:15.040 --> 00:02:17.110
She didn't look very happy.

02:17.160 --> 00:02:20.670
Then we both heard something behind us.

02:20.720 --> 00:02:25.110
On the road, we saw them.

02:25.160 --> 00:02:33.070
Those of them, the police, their clothes were black and they had battens.

02:33.120 --> 00:02:34.710
Nan looked at me.

02:34.760 --> 00:02:37.030
What are they?

02:37.080 --> 00:02:39.350
She asked.

02:39.400 --> 00:02:41.830
Police, Nan, it's the police.

02:41.880 --> 00:02:44.790
Are they here for us?

02:44.840 --> 00:02:46.430
She asked.

02:46.480 --> 00:02:50.470
No, Nan, not us, I said.

02:50.520 --> 00:02:52.430
Is it Jackie?

02:52.480 --> 00:02:53.430
Is it Tony?

02:53.480 --> 02:54.480
She asked.

02:54.560 --> 00:02:56.270
I didn't answer.

02:56.320 --> 00:02:58.990
I didn't want to know the answer.

02:59.040 --> 00:03:04.710
I took my Nan's arm and we walked slowly home.

03:04.760 --> 00:03:06.390
I loved to boogie.

03:06.440 --> 00:03:08.270
Geared above boogie.

03:08.320 --> 00:03:12.470
I'm trying to play cosmic boogie on the piano and thinking about ma'am.

03:12.520 --> 00:03:14.310
It was her piano.

03:14.360 --> 00:03:16.110
Ma'am's dead.

03:16.160 --> 00:03:18.310
She died two years ago.

03:18.360 --> 00:03:20.670
I think about her a lot.

03:20.720 --> 03:22.480
I've got a letter from her.

03:22.560 --> 00:03:25.230
She wrote it before she died.

03:25.280 --> 00:03:28.630
I'm still here, Billy, she wrote.

03:28.680 --> 00:03:30.390
But she isn't here.

03:30.440 --> 00:03:32.950
She's dead.

03:33.000 --> 00:03:34.790
Ma'am was good at the piano.

03:34.840 --> 00:03:36.670
She played for all of us.

03:36.720 --> 00:03:39.710
I'd like piano lessons, but they're too expensive.

03:39.760 --> 00:03:41.790
We haven't got the money.

03:41.840 --> 00:03:44.150
My dad's always telling us that.

03:44.200 --> 00:03:46.470
We haven't got much.

03:46.520 --> 00:03:49.310
Not now that there's a strike.

03:49.360 --> 03:51.120
Billy, stop that.

03:52.720 --> 00:03:54.350
It's Dad.

03:54.400 --> 00:03:57.190
He's going out again with Tony in a minute.

03:57.240 --> 00:03:59.150
Why do I have to stop?

03:59.200 --> 00:04:01.270
He's not going to be here.

04:01.320 --> 00:04:02.150
Why?

04:02.200 --> 00:04:03.790
Then I say the wrong thing.

04:03.840 --> 00:04:08.510
If it was ma'am, Dad comes over.

04:08.560 --> 00:04:11.190
He closes the piano with a bang.

04:11.240 --> 00:04:14.710
I'm not telling you again.

04:14.760 --> 00:04:16.910
I go to my room.

04:16.960 --> 04:18.760
Back to Tony's music.

04:22.480 --> 00:04:29.950
CHAPTER 2

04:30.000 --> 00:04:31.350
BILLY

04:31.400 --> 00:04:34.910
BOYS DON'T DO BILLY

04:34.960 --> 00:04:37.510
BILLY ELLIOT, this isn't a tea party.

04:37.560 --> 00:04:39.190
It's a boxing lesson.

04:39.240 --> 00:04:41.310
Heat him.

04:41.360 --> 00:04:45.550
It's Saturday morning, and I'm at the boxing club at the social.

04:45.600 --> 00:04:49.910
This morning, I'm against Greavesy, and he's bigger than me.

04:49.960 --> 00:04:52.390
I have my own ideas about boxing.

04:52.440 --> 00:04:54.630
It's all about your feet.

04:54.680 --> 00:04:57.110
So I run and turn and jump.

04:57.160 --> 00:04:58.990
I move quickly.

04:59.040 --> 00:05:01.790
Greavesy just stands there.

05:01.840 --> 00:05:04.630
George, the teacher, isn't happy.

05:04.680 --> 00:05:05.710
Heat him.

05:05.760 --> 00:05:07.830
Don't dance around.

05:07.880 --> 00:05:08.830
Bang.

05:08.880 --> 00:05:10.510
I'm on the floor.

05:10.560 --> 00:05:13.710
Greaves is standing over me and he's smiling.

05:13.760 --> 00:05:15.350
I can hear George.

05:15.400 --> 00:05:17.350
Billy Elliot, get up.

05:17.400 --> 00:05:19.510
You're going to do it right.

05:19.560 --> 00:05:22.350
You're not going home yet.

05:22.400 --> 00:05:23.870
I get up.

05:23.920 --> 00:05:26.310
George pulls me to the punch bag.

05:26.360 --> 00:05:28.030
Hit it.

05:28.080 --> 00:05:30.150
You're poor father.

05:30.200 --> 00:05:34.190
He pays for boxing lessons, and this happens.

05:34.240 --> 00:05:35.550
And on.

05:35.600 --> 00:05:36.990
And on.

05:37.040 --> 00:05:38.910
And on.

05:38.960 --> 00:05:41.230
I'm angry now.

05:41.280 --> 00:05:43.190
I hit the punch bag.

05:43.240 --> 00:05:47.270
I hate the punch bag.

05:47.320 --> 00:05:48.390
Arms up.

05:48.440 --> 00:05:49.150
And one.

05:49.200 --> 00:05:49.750
And two.

05:49.800 --> 00:05:50.350
And three.

05:50.400 --> 00:05:51.310
And four.

05:51.360 --> 00:05:54.230
Feel the music.

05:54.280 --> 00:05:58.350
On the other side of the room, there's a ballet class.

05:58.400 --> 00:06:00.950
Someone's playing the piano.

06:01.000 --> 00:06:04.710
One and two and three and four.

06:04.760 --> 00:06:08.590
As the music plays, I hit the punch bag.

06:08.640 --> 00:06:09.950
One and two.

06:10.000 --> 00:06:11.590
And bang and hit.

06:11.640 --> 00:06:13.150
And three and four.

06:13.200 --> 00:06:15.070
And hit and bang.

06:15.120 --> 00:06:17.910
That's better, George says.

06:17.960 --> 00:06:20.630
Stay here and get it right.

06:20.680 --> 00:06:22.630
See you next week.

06:22.680 --> 00:06:24.510
And he goes out.

06:24.560 --> 00:06:27.670
All the other boys go too.

06:27.720 --> 00:06:28.870
Right girls.

06:28.920 --> 00:06:30.510
And one and two.

06:30.560 --> 00:06:32.270
Debbie, don't look at me.

06:32.320 --> 00:06:33.950
Look in front of you.

06:34.000 --> 00:06:36.430
And three and four.

06:36.480 --> 00:06:38.230
I go and watch.

06:38.280 --> 00:06:39.910
It's clever.

06:39.960 --> 00:06:42.110
They all dance together.

06:42.160 --> 00:06:45.870
Left and two and down and two and turn and two.

06:45.920 --> 00:06:47.190
I try it.

06:47.240 --> 06:48.520
I stretch out my leg.

06:48.600 --> 00:06:51.550
Yeah, easy.

06:51.600 --> 00:06:53.430
Why don't you try?

06:53.480 --> 00:06:54.710
It's Debbie.

06:54.760 --> 00:06:56.470
She goes to my school.

06:56.520 --> 00:06:58.230
Nah, I say.

06:58.280 --> 00:07:00.430
Boys don't do ballet.

07:00.480 --> 00:07:02.390
Legs up.

07:02.440 --> 00:07:04.630
They all stretch their legs.

07:04.680 --> 00:07:11.030
Mrs. Wilkinson, she's the teacher, walks around and looks closely at each leg.

07:11.080 --> 00:07:13.070
I try it.

07:13.120 --> 00:07:14.870
Debbie laughs at me.

07:14.920 --> 00:07:17.150
Your legs moving.

07:17.200 --> 00:07:18.270
I look down.

07:18.320 --> 00:07:20.230
She's right.

07:20.280 --> 00:07:23.670
I'm wearing boxing shoes, I tell her.

07:23.720 --> 00:07:27.070
Mrs. Wilkinson takes a cigarette from her pocket.

07:27.120 --> 00:07:29.070
She smokes a lot.

07:29.120 --> 00:07:30.550
OK girls.

07:30.600 --> 00:07:34.750
And one and two and three and four.

07:34.800 --> 00:07:36.790
I want to do it too.

07:36.840 --> 00:07:39.070
I try, but it's difficult.

07:39.120 --> 00:07:41.230
I start to listen to the music.

07:41.280 --> 00:07:43.190
It's easier then.

07:43.240 --> 00:07:44.550
Shoes off.

07:44.600 --> 00:07:46.310
Mrs. in front of me.

07:46.360 --> 00:07:48.710
But not me, Miss, I start to say.

07:48.760 --> 00:07:51.350
But she's already walking down the room.

07:51.400 --> 00:07:54.230
I take off my shoes and then she's back again.

07:54.280 --> 00:07:56.230
With ballet shoes.

07:56.280 --> 00:07:58.190
Here you are, she says.

07:58.240 --> 00:08:00.830
You can't dance in boxing shoes.

08:00.880 --> 00:08:07.150
I don't know, but then I think, why not?

08:07.200 --> 00:08:08.630
So I do it.

08:08.680 --> 00:08:11.470
I do ballet for the first time.

08:11.520 --> 00:08:14.910
It isn't easy, but Miss is a good teacher.

08:14.960 --> 00:08:18.550
We're all standing on one leg with the other leg behind.

08:18.600 --> 00:08:20.750
Miss comes over.

08:20.800 --> 00:08:24.590
I like the leg, she says, and then walks off.

08:24.640 --> 00:08:28.190
She doesn't say much, but I'm happy.

08:28.240 --> 00:08:31.230
I'm walking home later and Miss drives by.

08:31.280 --> 00:08:33.910
She sees me and stops the car.

08:33.960 --> 00:08:36.390
Debbie's sitting in the back.

08:36.440 --> 00:08:37.510
Oh, I think.

08:37.560 --> 00:08:39.910
Debbie's her daughter.

08:39.960 --> 00:08:42.030
Miss is still smoking.

08:42.080 --> 00:08:43.990
She looks at me.

08:44.040 --> 00:08:46.390
It's 50p a lesson, you know.

08:46.440 --> 00:08:48.910
Bring me the money next week.

08:48.960 --> 00:08:49.990
I can't.

08:50.040 --> 00:08:51.430
I'm going to boxing.

08:51.480 --> 00:08:54.950
Your terrible at boxing says Debbie and laughs.

08:55.000 --> 00:08:56.830
Be quiet.

08:56.880 --> 00:09:00.270
Miss looks round at Debbie and then back at me.

09:00.320 --> 00:09:02.590
Didn't you enjoy it today?

09:02.640 --> 00:09:04.630
I don't say anything.

09:04.680 --> 00:09:08.350
It's your life, she says, and off they go.

09:08.400 --> 00:09:10.310
Miss was right.

09:10.360 --> 00:09:12.190
I enjoyed it.

09:12.240 --> 00:09:14.870
But the music was a bit boring.

09:14.920 --> 00:09:17.350
I think about Fred Astaire.

09:17.400 --> 00:09:19.150
My man loves him.

09:19.200 --> 00:09:20.750
He can dance.

09:20.800 --> 00:09:23.110
I want to dance like him.

09:23.160 --> 00:09:25.470
I run and jump down the road.

09:25.520 --> 00:09:28.870
Fred Astaire's music is playing in my head, and I feel great.

09:28.920 --> 00:09:44.310
Chapter 3, Billy, do the spin.

09:44.360 --> 00:09:47.390
I think about ballet all the time.

09:47.440 --> 00:09:50.270
One and two and up and down.

09:50.320 --> 00:09:54.310
Miss's words and the music are always in my head.

09:54.360 --> 00:09:55.990
But there's a problem.

09:56.040 --> 00:09:58.670
I feel stupid.

09:58.720 --> 00:10:00.550
And then there's my dad.

10:00.600 --> 00:10:04.350
And Tony, miners don't do ballet.

10:04.400 --> 00:10:07.510
Miners sons don't do ballet.

10:07.560 --> 00:10:11.830
Miners don't do much when they're on strike.

10:11.880 --> 00:10:14.030
The strike is going to end soon.

10:14.080 --> 00:10:16.070
I heard it on the TV.

10:16.120 --> 00:10:18.350
The cold weather's coming.

10:18.400 --> 00:10:22.830
The strikers and their families are going to be cold and hungry.

10:22.880 --> 00:10:25.150
They're going to need money.

10:25.200 --> 00:10:29.550
The strike is going to be over by Christmas.

10:29.600 --> 00:10:32.630
People know about the ballet at school, but I don't care.

10:32.680 --> 00:10:34.630
Some of the boys laugh at me.

10:34.680 --> 00:10:38.390
Hey, Billy, where are you pink ballet shoes today?

10:38.440 --> 00:10:40.470
What do they know?

10:40.520 --> 00:10:43.310
Debbie Wilkinson's always talking to me, too.

10:43.360 --> 00:10:47.270
She and her mama posh, not like my family.

10:47.320 --> 00:10:50.630
She walked home with me from school the other day.

10:50.680 --> 00:10:54.110
Lots of boys do ballet, you know, she said.

10:54.160 --> 00:10:56.230
Don't be stupid, who?

10:56.280 --> 00:10:58.270
Who do we know?

10:58.320 --> 00:11:01.150
No one here, but lots of men do it.

11:01.200 --> 00:11:03.470
Are you coming next week?

11:03.520 --> 00:11:04.870
She looked at me.

11:04.920 --> 00:11:06.270
I'm going to boxing.

11:06.320 --> 00:11:09.750
My dad says, I said, I was a bit angry.

11:09.800 --> 00:11:11.070
OK.

11:11.120 --> 00:11:12.790
She walked off.

11:12.840 --> 00:11:17.830
She lives in the nice part of town, in a posh house with a posh garden.

11:17.880 --> 00:11:21.630
Her and her mom don't know anything about our life.

11:21.680 --> 00:11:24.510
Then the music comes back in my head.

11:24.560 --> 11:28.280
I start to dance, and I forget about my life, too.

11:30.920 --> 00:11:32.910
I've got this friend, Michael.

11:32.960 --> 00:11:36.750
He hates football, not like me.

11:36.800 --> 00:11:40.070
We're different, but we're best friends.

11:40.120 --> 00:11:42.190
I can talk to him about things.

11:42.240 --> 00:11:44.310
I told him about the ballet.

11:44.360 --> 00:11:45.950
I did some of the moves.

11:46.000 --> 00:11:47.550
He thinks it's cool.

11:47.600 --> 00:11:49.830
Leg out, arm out, one, two, I said.

11:49.880 --> 00:11:51.350
Eyes to the front.

11:51.400 --> 00:11:52.550
Michael laughed.

11:52.600 --> 00:11:54.630
Oh, when's the next lesson?

11:54.680 --> 00:11:56.390
I'm not going, I said.

11:56.440 --> 00:11:57.870
Bal is for girls.

11:57.920 --> 00:11:59.510
I feel stupid.

11:59.560 --> 00:12:02.070
You are stupid, Michael laughed.

12:02.120 --> 00:12:04.190
Anyway, it's not just for girls.

12:04.240 --> 00:12:05.230
It's different for men.

12:05.280 --> 00:12:07.510
Men are stronger.

12:07.560 --> 00:12:09.230
He was right.

12:09.280 --> 00:12:15.070
I can jump higher than the girls in the ballet class, and I'm better than most of them.

12:15.120 --> 00:12:17.030
So I went again.

12:17.080 --> 00:12:22.550
On Saturday, I took my 50p from the kitchen table, and I went to the social.

12:22.600 --> 00:12:25.310
This week, the class was in a different room.

12:25.360 --> 00:12:28.790
That was good because I didn't want to see George.

12:28.840 --> 00:12:31.310
At the start, it was boring.

12:31.360 --> 00:12:33.950
I didn't know the moves, so I stopped.

12:34.000 --> 00:12:35.950
Miss came over.

12:36.000 --> 00:12:37.670
What are you doing?

12:37.720 --> 00:12:39.990
I don't know the moves, Miss, I said.

12:40.040 --> 00:12:41.350
Follow the girls.

12:41.400 --> 00:12:43.230
Go to the back and watch them.

12:43.280 --> 00:12:46.750
And one, two, three.

12:46.800 --> 00:12:50.430
That was OK, but it was still a bit boring.

12:50.480 --> 00:12:52.350
Then Miss showed us the spin.

12:52.400 --> 00:12:56.190
You spin around and around very fast, and then you stop.

12:56.240 --> 00:12:58.430
You must stay in the same place.

12:58.480 --> 00:13:00.630
It looks great, but it's very difficult.

13:00.680 --> 00:13:02.310
You fall on the floor a lot.

13:02.360 --> 00:13:04.230
We all tried it.

13:04.280 --> 00:13:06.350
Do it at home, Miss said.

13:06.400 --> 00:13:07.990
Try again and again.

13:08.040 --> 00:13:10.430
You can do it.

13:10.480 --> 00:13:13.590
At the end of the class, Miss came over to me.

13:13.640 --> 00:13:16.550
So are you coming next week?

13:16.600 --> 00:13:18.590
I don't know, Miss.

13:18.640 --> 00:13:20.790
She looks at my ballet shoes.

13:20.840 --> 00:13:23.590
Give me those, then.

13:23.640 --> 00:13:24.990
I didn't want to.

13:25.040 --> 00:13:28.030
I wanted to learn the spin and do it at boxing.

13:28.080 --> 00:13:30.950
I wanted to see George's face.

13:31.000 --> 00:13:34.990
No, it's OK, I said, and gave him a 50p.

13:35.040 --> 00:13:37.350
She took it and went off.

13:37.400 --> 00:13:39.990
She didn't say anything.

13:40.040 --> 00:13:43.430
At home, Nan was in the kitchen.

13:43.480 --> 00:13:45.110
Ballet shoes.

13:45.160 --> 00:13:46.390
How lovely.

13:46.440 --> 00:13:51.230
She said, don't tell Dad, I said, and ran into my room.

13:51.280 --> 00:13:54.390
Luckily, Dad and Tony were out.

13:54.440 --> 00:13:58.590
Dad is not going to understand about ballet shoes.

13:58.640 --> 00:14:02.630
Dad isn't going to understand about any of this.

14:02.680 --> 00:14:05.830
I put the ballet shoes under my bed with my boxing things.

14:05.880 --> 00:14:08.910
Anyway, I'm going to go to boxing soon.

14:08.960 --> 14:11.960
I'm going to go when I can do the spin.

14:12.080 --> 00:14:20.950
MUSIC

14:21.000 --> 00:14:26.430
Chapter 4, Jackie, my son Billy.

14:26.480 --> 00:14:30.270
There's something funny about Billy at the moment.

14:30.320 --> 00:14:32.750
He's a bit different from the other boys.

14:32.800 --> 00:14:34.150
I know that.

14:34.200 --> 00:14:37.590
But now, it's this spinning.

14:37.640 --> 00:14:39.430
He does it everywhere.

14:39.480 --> 00:14:43.070
He puts out his arms and spins around and around.

14:43.120 --> 00:14:46.870
He looks a bit stupid, like a girl.

14:46.920 --> 00:14:50.190
He doesn't care, not Billy.

14:50.240 --> 00:14:52.990
It's a boxing move, he tells me.

14:53.040 --> 00:14:54.910
Boxing.

14:54.960 --> 00:14:58.150
Sometimes, I can't believe Billy is my son.

14:58.200 --> 00:15:01.590
Then, there's the strike.

15:01.640 --> 00:15:04.150
We started four months ago.

15:04.200 --> 00:15:06.230
We're so poor now.

15:06.280 --> 00:15:09.150
We haven't got money for anything.

15:09.200 --> 00:15:11.190
What's going to happen?

15:11.240 --> 00:15:12.750
We don't know.

15:12.800 --> 00:15:15.710
Maybe they're going to close the mines.

15:15.760 --> 00:15:18.670
Maybe they decided a long time ago.

15:18.720 --> 00:15:21.590
So why are we doing this?

15:21.640 --> 00:15:22.870
Tone is angry.

15:22.920 --> 00:15:27.030
I see it in his eyes every day at the mine.

15:27.080 --> 00:15:30.790
What's it going to do if there's no mine?

15:30.840 --> 00:15:33.070
Some men choose to work.

15:33.120 --> 00:15:35.550
We call them scabs.

15:35.600 --> 15:38.440
The strikers stand together at the mine.

15:38.520 --> 00:15:40.830
The scabs go through in buses.

15:40.880 --> 00:15:43.150
There are police everywhere.

15:43.200 --> 00:15:44.790
We shout at the buses.

15:44.840 --> 00:15:46.670
We bang on the windows.

15:46.720 --> 00:15:48.670
The scabs look frightened.

15:48.720 --> 00:15:50.990
I'm not surprised.

15:51.040 --> 00:15:53.590
This morning, I was next to George.

15:53.640 --> 00:15:54.950
It was cold.

15:55.000 --> 00:15:57.510
We waited for the scab buses.

15:57.560 --> 00:15:59.670
Listen, Jackie, he said.

15:59.720 --> 00:16:01.110
Forget the money.

16:01.160 --> 00:16:03.030
The 50P for the boxing.

16:03.080 --> 00:16:05.390
I don't do it for the money.

16:05.440 --> 00:16:07.070
What?

16:07.120 --> 00:16:09.510
I didn't understand.

16:09.560 --> 00:16:11.230
It's Billy.

16:11.280 --> 00:16:13.350
He doesn't come to boxing now.

16:13.400 --> 00:16:15.910
Is it because of the money?

16:15.960 --> 00:16:18.110
I started to think.

16:18.160 --> 00:16:21.550
Where did Billy go every Saturday morning?

16:21.600 --> 00:16:23.950
Then a bus came in and everyone started a shout.

16:24.000 --> 00:16:27.670
Scab, scab, scab.

16:27.720 --> 00:16:29.790
I shouted with the other men.

16:29.840 --> 00:16:32.670
But I thought about other things.

16:32.720 --> 00:16:34.710
Tomorrow was Saturday.

16:34.760 --> 00:16:37.150
Billy's boxing day.

16:37.200 --> 16:38.240
I had an idea.

16:47.840 --> 00:16:49.310
Chapter 5.

16:49.360 --> 00:16:52.310
Billy, just you and me.

16:52.360 --> 00:16:54.030
I can spin now.

16:54.080 --> 00:16:56.750
I can do everything, all the moves.

16:56.800 --> 00:16:59.430
Miss teaches me for a lot of the lesson.

16:59.480 --> 00:17:02.470
The girls aren't happy about it.

17:02.520 --> 00:17:04.190
Miss, what about us?

17:04.240 --> 00:17:05.830
They say.

17:05.880 --> 00:17:07.070
She doesn't listen.

17:07.120 --> 00:17:09.110
I'm busy.

17:09.160 --> 00:17:10.990
Then it happened.

17:11.040 --> 00:17:14.470
Michael often said to me, what about your dad?

17:14.520 --> 00:17:16.350
What are you going to do?

17:16.400 --> 00:17:18.870
Yeah, it happened.

17:18.920 --> 00:17:21.270
I was in the center of the class.

17:21.320 --> 00:17:23.230
Miss was next to me.

17:23.280 --> 00:17:25.750
And stretch your leg, Billy.

17:25.800 --> 00:17:27.390
I looked up.

17:27.440 --> 00:17:29.710
And there he was by the door.

17:29.760 --> 00:17:32.070
His face was red.

17:32.120 --> 00:17:33.950
Miss all in two.

17:34.000 --> 00:17:36.390
The music stopped.

17:36.440 --> 00:17:40.070
You out now, he shouted.

17:40.120 --> 00:17:43.230
Miss wanted to say something, but I stopped her.

17:43.280 --> 00:17:45.350
I had enough problems.

17:45.400 --> 00:17:49.710
I followed Dad out of the social.

17:49.760 --> 00:17:51.230
Billy?

17:51.280 --> 00:17:52.870
We were in the kitchen.

17:52.920 --> 00:17:55.390
Dad didn't speak to me when we left the social.

17:55.440 --> 00:17:57.390
Maybe he was too angry.

17:57.440 --> 00:17:59.110
I don't know.

17:59.160 --> 00:18:00.630
What's wrong with Billy?

18:00.680 --> 00:18:03.790
I said, lots of people do it.

18:03.840 --> 00:18:06.350
Dad's face was red again.

18:06.400 --> 00:18:09.750
Lots of girls do ballet, Billy, not boys.

18:09.800 --> 00:18:12.910
Boys do football or boxing.

18:12.960 --> 00:18:14.830
It was true in a way.

18:14.880 --> 00:18:16.590
Ballet isn't boxing.

18:16.640 --> 00:18:18.790
You don't hit anyone.

18:18.840 --> 00:18:20.750
It's not mining.

18:20.800 --> 00:18:23.470
So my dad can't understand it.

18:23.520 --> 00:18:26.030
So it's not boxing or mining.

18:26.080 --> 00:18:27.550
Well, so what?

18:27.600 --> 00:18:29.270
I'm not the same as my dad.

18:29.320 --> 00:18:31.510
I can be different.

18:31.560 --> 00:18:33.510
I like dancing, Dad.

18:33.560 --> 00:18:34.630
That's all it is.

18:34.680 --> 00:18:35.630
Dancing.

18:35.680 --> 00:18:37.670
Why is that so bad?

18:37.720 --> 00:18:39.710
Listen, forget about dancing.

18:39.760 --> 00:18:40.830
You're not doing it.

18:40.880 --> 00:18:42.790
Understand?

18:42.840 --> 00:18:45.270
I jumped up and shouted in his face.

18:45.320 --> 00:18:46.790
I hate you.

18:46.840 --> 00:18:48.270
I run out of the house.

18:48.320 --> 00:18:49.430
I ran and ran.

18:49.480 --> 00:18:51.550
I hated my dad.

18:51.600 --> 00:18:54.310
I loved dancing, and I was good at it.

18:54.360 --> 00:18:55.870
I knew that.

18:55.920 --> 00:18:58.070
Miss knew it too.

18:58.120 --> 00:18:59.670
Suddenly, I wanted to see her.

18:59.720 --> 00:19:04.790
I was in Mrs. House.

19:04.840 --> 00:19:05.990
It was funny.

19:06.040 --> 00:19:09.830
Me, Debbie, Miss, and her husband.

19:09.880 --> 00:19:11.630
He was funny too.

19:11.680 --> 00:19:14.070
It was always in the pub, Debbie said.

19:14.120 --> 00:19:16.070
He always had a beer in his hand.

19:16.120 --> 00:19:19.030
Oh, it's little Jean Kelly.

19:19.080 --> 00:19:20.270
He said when he saw me.

19:20.320 --> 00:19:23.030
Be quiet, Tom, Miss said.

19:23.080 --> 00:19:25.510
You're not in the pub now?

19:25.560 --> 19:27.400
I had dinner with them.

19:27.480 --> 00:19:30.790
Later, Miss took me home in her car.

19:30.840 --> 00:19:34.390
She stopped near my house and looked at me.

19:34.440 --> 00:19:38.750
Billy, I'm thinking about the Royal Ballet School.

19:38.800 --> 00:19:41.190
Aren't you a bit old, Miss, I said?

19:41.240 --> 00:19:43.110
Not me, you.

19:43.160 --> 00:19:47.430
There's an audition a new castle in two weeks.

19:47.480 --> 00:19:48.990
Ballet School.

19:49.040 --> 00:19:50.550
Me.

19:50.600 --> 00:19:52.470
Ballet.

19:52.520 --> 00:19:54.190
All day.

19:54.240 --> 00:19:57.150
Every day.

19:57.200 --> 00:20:01.350
Can you do Ballet as a job, then, Miss, I asked her?

20:01.400 --> 00:20:04.550
Yes, if you're good enough.

20:04.600 --> 00:20:06.870
But I don't know anything.

20:06.920 --> 00:20:09.990
Look, she took a cigarette from her bag.

20:10.040 --> 00:20:11.270
They teach you.

20:11.320 --> 00:20:15.030
It's a school, and she waited a minute.

20:15.080 --> 00:20:17.950
I think you're good enough.

20:18.000 --> 00:20:19.870
Wow.

20:19.920 --> 00:20:22.630
She didn't usually say anything nice.

20:22.680 --> 20:25.000
What about my dad?

20:25.080 --> 00:20:27.390
I can speak to him if you want.

20:27.440 --> 00:20:29.830
No, please, Miss.

20:29.880 --> 00:20:32.670
I knew my dad.

20:32.720 --> 00:20:35.110
I can give you more lessons, she said.

20:35.160 --> 00:20:36.590
Just you and me.

20:36.640 --> 00:20:37.990
Don't think about the money.

20:38.040 --> 00:20:40.430
I'm not doing it for the money.

20:40.480 --> 00:20:41.870
I thought about it.

20:41.920 --> 00:20:45.350
My dad didn't know about it, and that was wrong.

20:45.400 --> 00:20:48.350
But I wanted to be a dancer.

20:48.400 --> 00:20:50.150
I smiled at Miss.

20:50.200 --> 00:20:51.790
OK, then.

20:51.840 --> 00:20:53.550
She smiled, too.

20:53.600 --> 00:20:56.470
She didn't usually smile.

20:56.520 --> 00:20:59.630
6 o'clock on Monday at the social, she said.

20:59.680 --> 00:21:00.830
OK.

21:00.880 --> 00:21:02.550
I opened the car door.

21:02.600 --> 00:21:05.870
Oh, and Billy, bring something with you.

21:05.920 --> 00:21:08.030
Something that's important to you.

21:08.080 --> 00:21:10.470
We must think of an idea for the audition dance.

21:10.520 --> 00:21:25.750
Chapter 6, Billy, Mam's Dance.

21:25.800 --> 00:21:27.910
There wasn't much time.

21:27.960 --> 00:21:30.670
The audition was in two weeks.

21:30.720 --> 00:21:32.630
I met Miss almost every night.

21:32.680 --> 00:21:37.150
I'm going to Michael's house, I told Dad.

21:37.200 --> 00:21:40.350
The first evening, I had some things with me.

21:40.400 --> 00:21:45.590
My football, some T-Rex music, I liked to boogie.

21:45.640 --> 00:21:48.870
It was Tony's, I didn't ask him.

21:48.920 --> 00:21:52.390
Then there was the letter from my mom.

21:52.440 --> 00:21:54.590
Miss started to read the letter.

21:54.640 --> 00:21:57.190
Dear Billy, she stopped.

21:57.240 --> 00:21:59.550
Can I read this, Billy?

21:59.600 --> 00:22:01.830
Yeah, I said.

22:01.880 --> 00:22:04.350
I'm still here, Billy.

22:04.400 --> 00:22:06.030
You can't see me.

22:06.080 --> 00:22:07.030
But I am.

22:07.080 --> 00:22:09.030
I'm always with you.

22:09.080 --> 00:22:10.910
Don't forget that.

22:10.960 --> 00:22:12.430
And I love you.

22:12.480 --> 00:22:17.270
Be true to Billy Elliot, all your life.

22:17.320 --> 00:22:19.270
Miss looked away and didn't say anything.

22:19.320 --> 00:22:23.350
You OK, Miss, I asked.

22:23.400 --> 00:22:26.870
She's going to cry, I thought.

22:26.920 --> 00:22:29.390
She was a very special person, Billy.

22:29.440 --> 00:22:35.390
She said, nah, she was just my mom, I said.

22:35.440 --> 00:22:38.990
What did your mom like doing, chest me?

22:39.040 --> 00:22:41.270
She liked music, I said.

22:41.320 --> 00:22:43.670
And then we listened to the T-Rex music.

22:43.720 --> 00:22:45.430
I liked to boogie.

22:45.480 --> 00:22:47.510
Gee her bug boogie.

22:47.560 --> 00:22:49.270
I liked to boogie.

22:49.320 --> 00:22:52.110
On a Saturday night.

22:52.160 --> 00:22:55.190
It's happy music, Miss said.

22:55.240 --> 00:22:57.150
Dance music.

22:57.200 --> 00:22:59.430
And your mom liked this.

22:59.480 --> 00:23:00.870
I?

23:00.920 --> 00:23:02.910
Then this is our dance, Billy.

23:02.960 --> 00:23:04.670
Let's go.

23:04.720 --> 00:23:07.470
We danced and jumped and ran around.

23:07.520 --> 00:23:09.910
We thought of lots of new moves.

23:09.960 --> 00:23:12.990
Now, think about your mom, Miss said.

23:13.040 --> 00:23:14.110
She's watching you.

23:14.160 --> 00:23:17.070
She's smiling and laughing.

23:17.120 --> 00:23:18.750
And it worked.

23:18.800 --> 00:23:21.670
I thought about mom, and I did a great spin.

23:21.720 --> 23:22.880
I was on top of the world.

23:25.880 --> 00:23:28.870
At home, things were very different.

23:28.920 --> 00:23:31.510
No one was on top of the world.

23:31.560 --> 00:23:35.030
There were police all over the town.

23:35.080 --> 00:23:37.190
They frightened me.

23:37.240 --> 00:23:39.590
Tony was never frightened.

23:39.640 --> 00:23:41.870
He shouted a lot at Dad.

23:41.920 --> 00:23:43.630
What's wrong with you?

23:43.680 --> 00:23:46.670
This strike is our only hope.

23:46.720 --> 00:23:48.750
Dad didn't answer.

23:48.800 --> 00:23:51.950
He just sat there and said nothing.

23:52.000 --> 00:23:55.110
I was sorry for him.

23:55.160 --> 00:24:00.590
Tonight, I'm in bed, and I hear something in the kitchen.

24:00.640 --> 00:24:02.870
It's Dad and Tony.

24:02.920 --> 24:04.760
I sit up and listen.

24:04.800 --> 00:24:07.510
Tony sounds very angry.

24:07.560 --> 00:24:11.430
I'm not going to sit at home and do nothing, he shouts.

24:11.480 --> 00:24:14.350
You think it's the end, but for me, it's the start.

24:14.400 --> 00:24:16.590
Now move.

24:16.640 --> 00:24:18.630
I run into the kitchen.

24:18.680 --> 00:24:21.710
Tony has a button, a police button.

24:21.760 --> 00:24:23.110
Where did he get that?

24:23.160 --> 00:24:25.470
What's he going to do with it?

24:25.520 --> 00:24:27.510
This time, Dad shouts back.

24:27.560 --> 00:24:29.110
You're not going.

24:29.160 --> 00:24:31.230
And you're not going to use that.

24:31.280 --> 00:24:32.790
He's looking at the button.

24:32.840 --> 00:24:34.590
Forget about the police.

24:34.640 --> 00:24:35.830
They're doing a job.

24:35.880 --> 00:24:37.950
That's all.

24:38.000 --> 00:24:40.670
Try and stop me then, says Tony.

24:40.720 --> 00:24:42.070
You can't do anything.

24:42.120 --> 00:24:43.590
You're nothing.

24:43.640 --> 00:24:47.510
Without ma'am, you're nothing.

24:47.560 --> 00:24:49.270
They're by the back door.

24:49.320 --> 00:24:51.870
Dad's face is white.

24:51.920 --> 00:24:54.030
Suddenly, he hits Tony.

24:54.080 --> 00:24:55.950
Crack.

24:56.000 --> 00:24:58.550
Tony falls to the floor.

24:58.600 --> 00:24:59.790
Stop it.

24:59.840 --> 00:25:00.630
Stop it.

25:00.680 --> 00:25:02.710
I shout.

25:02.760 --> 00:25:05.190
Tony gets up slowly.

25:05.240 --> 00:25:07.310
He doesn't say a word.

25:07.360 --> 00:25:09.430
He doesn't look at Dad.

25:09.480 --> 00:25:12.430
He just runs out of the door.

25:12.480 --> 00:25:15.190
The button is under his arm.

25:15.240 --> 25:16.920
Dad doesn't stop him this time.

25:26.680 --> 00:25:31.790
Chapter 7, Billy Black Friday.

25:31.840 --> 00:25:33.950
Billy, you're not trying.

25:34.000 --> 00:25:35.750
Arm up.

25:35.800 --> 00:25:37.230
What?

25:37.280 --> 00:25:38.910
I'm at the social with miss.

25:38.960 --> 00:25:42.310
But I can only think about last night and my dad and Tony.

25:42.360 --> 00:25:44.270
Eyes to the front.

25:44.320 --> 00:25:45.070
Bang.

25:45.120 --> 00:25:46.790
Dad hits Tony.

25:46.840 --> 00:25:48.550
Do it again, Billy.

25:48.600 --> 00:25:49.190
Bang.

25:49.240 --> 00:25:50.830
Tony's on the floor.

25:50.880 --> 00:25:53.430
Billy, that's not good enough.

25:53.480 --> 00:25:54.830
I can't.

25:54.880 --> 00:25:56.710
Suddenly, I hate her.

25:56.760 --> 00:25:59.910
She's standing right next to me and smoking in my face.

25:59.960 --> 00:26:01.750
Do it again, she says.

26:01.800 --> 00:26:03.350
No.

26:03.400 --> 00:26:04.630
What?

26:04.680 --> 00:26:06.670
She can't believe it.

26:06.720 --> 00:26:09.630
Suddenly, I am angry about everything.

26:09.680 --> 00:26:14.270
Last night, the audition, everything's going wrong.

26:14.320 --> 00:26:16.190
Tony was right about one thing.

26:16.240 --> 00:26:18.790
Without ma'am, we're all nothing.

26:18.840 --> 00:26:21.630
And she's never coming back.

26:21.680 --> 00:26:23.110
I run out of the room.

26:23.160 --> 00:26:24.830
Miss follows me.

26:24.880 --> 00:26:27.270
Billy, I'm sorry, she says.

26:27.320 --> 00:26:28.990
I want to help you.

26:29.040 --> 26:30.240
No, you don't.

26:30.320 --> 00:26:31.510
The audition's for you.

26:31.560 --> 00:26:32.710
Not for me.

26:32.760 --> 00:26:35.830
That's not true, she says.

26:35.880 --> 00:26:37.470
I can't stop now.

26:37.520 --> 00:26:38.550
What have you got?

26:38.600 --> 00:26:39.590
Nothing.

26:39.640 --> 00:26:40.830
No dance school.

26:40.880 --> 00:26:41.670
What are you?

26:41.720 --> 00:26:42.750
You're nothing.

26:42.800 --> 00:26:44.910
Don't speak to me like that.

26:44.960 --> 00:26:47.150
Then she hits me across the face.

26:47.200 --> 00:26:49.270
She looks very surprised.

26:49.320 --> 00:26:51.310
I'm surprised, too.

26:51.360 --> 00:26:52.510
I want to run.

26:52.560 --> 00:26:55.350
But I can't leave.

26:55.400 --> 00:26:57.590
I must dance.

26:57.640 --> 00:27:01.790
And because I can't leave, I start to cry.

27:01.840 --> 00:27:03.950
She puts out her arms.

27:04.000 --> 00:27:06.110
I'm sorry, Billy.

27:06.160 --> 00:27:09.830
And I cry in her arms for about five minutes.

27:09.880 --> 00:27:12.590
I can't stop.

27:12.640 --> 00:27:14.670
Right, she says.

27:14.720 --> 00:27:16.590
Is that enough?

27:16.640 --> 00:27:18.670
Yes, I say.

27:18.720 --> 00:27:20.630
Sorry, Miss.

27:20.680 --> 27:24.040
Right, then, she says, let's start again.

27:25.040 --> 00:27:28.990
There was something different about that Friday.

27:29.040 --> 00:27:31.990
Black Friday, Dad called it.

27:32.040 --> 00:27:34.990
The audition was the next morning.

27:35.040 --> 00:27:37.990
I walked home after my last lesson with Miss.

27:38.040 --> 00:27:39.990
I was happy.

27:40.040 --> 00:27:42.990
I did my audition dance in my head.

27:43.040 --> 00:27:45.990
Then I turned into our road.

27:46.040 --> 00:27:47.990
And saw them all.

27:48.040 --> 00:27:50.990
There were police everywhere.

27:51.040 --> 00:27:52.990
Mrs. Watts lives near us.

27:53.040 --> 00:27:54.990
She saw me and pulled me into her house.

27:55.040 --> 00:27:56.990
Get in, Billy.

27:57.040 --> 00:27:58.990
What's happening?

27:59.040 --> 00:27:59.990
It's your Tony.

28:00.040 --> 00:28:00.990
He's in trouble.

28:01.040 --> 00:28:02.990
The police wants him.

28:03.040 --> 00:28:03.990
Tony?

28:04.040 --> 00:28:06.990
I didn't understand.

28:07.040 --> 00:28:08.990
Where did he go at night?

28:09.040 --> 00:28:10.990
What did he do?

28:11.040 --> 00:28:15.990
My dad and Tony, especially Tony, hate the police.

28:16.040 --> 00:28:19.990
Now, I understand.

28:20.040 --> 00:28:21.990
I saw one man.

28:22.040 --> 00:28:24.990
He was in front of one of the police.

28:25.040 --> 00:28:27.990
The policeman hit him with his baton.

28:28.040 --> 00:28:29.990
He didn't stop.

28:30.040 --> 00:28:32.990
He hit him again and again.

28:33.040 --> 00:28:34.990
Then I saw our Tony.

28:35.040 --> 00:28:38.990
He ran up the road with the police all around him.

28:39.040 --> 00:28:40.990
They were faster than him.

28:41.040 --> 00:28:41.990
I ran to the door.

28:42.040 --> 00:28:43.990
Tony, in here.

28:44.040 --> 00:28:45.990
He didn't hear me.

28:46.040 --> 00:28:46.990
It was too loud.

28:47.040 --> 00:28:47.990
Everyone shouted.

28:48.040 --> 00:28:50.990
Batons banged on doors.

28:51.040 --> 00:28:54.990
After that, I saw about 20 police, all together.

28:55.040 --> 28:58.040
And our Tony was under them.

29:07.040 --> 00:29:09.990
Chapter 8, Tony.

29:10.040 --> 00:29:11.990
Happy Christmas.

29:12.040 --> 00:29:14.990
I stared in the police station that night.

29:15.040 --> 00:29:16.990
There was no bed.

29:17.040 --> 00:29:18.990
Where do I sleep?

29:19.040 --> 00:29:19.990
I asked.

29:20.040 --> 00:29:21.990
They laughed.

29:22.040 --> 00:29:23.990
I was black and blue.

29:24.040 --> 00:29:26.990
I hate the police.

29:27.040 --> 00:29:29.990
Next morning, I sat in the courtroom.

29:30.040 --> 00:29:32.990
There was a big policeman next to me.

29:33.040 --> 00:29:35.990
I saw Dad and our Billy.

29:36.040 --> 00:29:38.990
Dad was angry, but he didn't say anything.

29:39.040 --> 00:29:41.990
It was over very quickly.

29:42.040 --> 00:29:45.990
Pay the court 100 pounds, they said.

29:46.040 --> 00:29:46.990
We haven't got any money.

29:47.040 --> 00:29:48.990
They know that.

29:49.040 --> 00:29:52.990
And our happy Christmas to you too, I shouted.

29:53.040 --> 00:29:56.990
Get out of here, said the policeman.

29:57.040 --> 00:29:57.990
We walked home.

29:58.040 --> 00:30:00.990
Me, Dad and Billy.

30:01.040 --> 00:30:03.990
I wanted to get home and go to bed.

30:04.040 --> 00:30:06.990
I wanted to cry like a little boy.

30:07.040 --> 00:30:09.990
But there was this woman in front of our house.

30:10.040 --> 00:30:11.990
Who's that?

30:12.040 --> 00:30:12.990
I asked.

30:13.040 --> 00:30:14.990
She came up to Billy.

30:15.040 --> 00:30:16.990
Did she know him?

30:17.040 --> 00:30:18.990
Where were you, Billy?

30:19.040 --> 00:30:20.990
What happened?

30:21.040 --> 00:30:24.990
Billy didn't want to say anything, but she waited.

30:25.040 --> 00:30:28.990
Our Tony was in court, he said quietly.

30:29.040 --> 00:30:29.990
I went too.

30:30.040 --> 00:30:32.990
He didn't look at her.

30:33.040 --> 00:30:35.990
Our Dad looked at Billy and this woman.

30:36.040 --> 00:30:38.990
Did he know her too?

30:39.040 --> 00:30:41.990
What's going on, I thought?

30:42.040 --> 00:30:43.990
Let's go in, Dad said.

30:44.040 --> 00:30:45.990
What's all this about, I said?

30:46.040 --> 00:30:47.990
I didn't want this.

30:48.040 --> 00:30:49.990
Things were bad enough.

30:50.040 --> 00:30:51.990
I didn't like this woman.

30:52.040 --> 00:30:52.990
She was posh.

30:53.040 --> 00:30:54.990
She had posh clothes.

30:55.040 --> 00:30:56.990
She wasn't like us.

30:57.040 --> 00:30:58.990
We went into the living room.

30:59.040 --> 00:31:00.990
Billy didn't look very happy.

31:01.040 --> 00:31:03.990
He's in trouble, I thought.

31:04.040 --> 00:31:05.990
Then she started.

31:06.040 --> 00:31:09.990
Today, Billy had an audition for the Royal Ballet School.

31:10.040 --> 00:31:12.990
I know things are difficult, but...

31:13.040 --> 00:31:14.990
I didn't believe my ears.

31:15.040 --> 00:31:15.990
I laughed.

31:16.040 --> 00:31:17.990
I looked at Billy and laughed again.

31:18.040 --> 00:31:18.990
What?

31:19.040 --> 00:31:20.990
Ballet, I said.

31:21.040 --> 00:31:24.990
I went over to the woman and shouted in her face.

31:25.040 --> 00:31:28.990
My brother does not do ballet, you stupid woman.

31:29.040 --> 00:31:32.990
My brother is not going to do ballet.

31:33.040 --> 00:31:34.990
Her face was white.

31:35.040 --> 00:31:37.990
She was frightened, but she didn't move.

31:38.040 --> 00:31:40.990
Don't shout at me, she said.

31:41.040 --> 00:31:42.990
Billy's a very good dancer.

31:43.040 --> 00:31:45.990
Where does he go after school every day?

31:46.040 --> 00:31:47.990
You don't know, and you don't care.

31:48.040 --> 00:31:49.990
I wanted to hit her.

31:50.040 --> 00:31:52.990
She knew, but she didn't care.

31:53.040 --> 00:31:54.990
Is Billy going to be like you?

31:55.040 --> 00:31:55.990
She said to me.

31:56.040 --> 00:31:57.990
No job, no hope.

31:58.040 --> 00:31:59.990
Do you want that for Billy?

32:00.040 --> 00:32:02.990
He's not going to be a scab, I shouted.

32:03.040 --> 00:32:04.990
Look at him.

32:05.040 --> 00:32:05.990
He's only twelve.

32:06.040 --> 00:32:06.990
He's a child.

32:07.040 --> 00:32:09.990
And you're putting stupid ideas in his head.

32:10.040 --> 00:32:12.990
You learn better when you're young, said Billy.

32:13.040 --> 00:32:14.990
Shut it, I shouted at him.

32:15.040 --> 00:32:15.990
I turned back to her.

32:16.040 --> 00:32:20.990
My brother is not running around in a stupid dress for you or anyone.

32:21.040 --> 00:32:22.990
It's not for me, she said.

32:23.040 --> 00:32:24.990
It's for Billy.

32:25.040 --> 00:32:25.990
And then she turned to Billy.

32:26.040 --> 00:32:28.990
See you Billy, she said, and walked out of the house.

32:29.040 --> 00:32:31.990
Get out of our house, I shouted at her.

32:32.040 --> 00:32:33.990
And don't come back.

32:34.040 --> 00:32:35.990
She didn't hear.

32:36.040 --> 00:32:37.990
I wanted to hit Billy then.

32:38.040 --> 00:32:39.990
I wanted to hit someone.

32:40.040 --> 00:32:41.990
But he was behind our dad.

32:42.040 --> 00:32:43.990
Shut up.

32:44.040 --> 00:32:44.990
I hate you.

32:45.040 --> 00:32:45.990
He shouted at me.

32:46.040 --> 00:32:46.990
I looked at him.

32:47.040 --> 00:32:48.990
He's right.

32:49.040 --> 00:32:50.990
He hates me, I thought.

32:51.040 --> 00:32:51.990
You little.

32:52.040 --> 00:32:53.990
I tried to hit him, but dad stopped me.

32:54.040 --> 00:32:56.990
Billy ran out of the back door.

32:57.040 --> 00:32:57.990
I looked at dad.

32:58.040 --> 00:33:00.990
I'm going to the pub, I said.

33:01.040 --> 00:33:02.990
I bang the door on my way out.

33:03.040 --> 33:06.040
And if I see that posh woman again.

33:09.040 --> 00:33:15.990
Chapter 9.

33:16.040 --> 00:33:18.990
Billy, you're in trouble now.

33:19.040 --> 00:33:23.990
That was the worst Christmas of my life, I said.

33:24.040 --> 00:33:25.990
I was with Michael.

33:26.040 --> 00:33:28.990
It was the day after Christmas, and we were out in the cold.

33:29.040 --> 00:33:30.990
No Christmas tree.

33:31.040 --> 00:33:32.990
No nothing.

33:33.040 --> 00:33:34.990
And no man.

33:35.040 --> 00:33:36.990
Have some of this.

33:37.040 --> 00:33:38.990
He had some of his dad's beer.

33:39.040 --> 00:33:39.990
I tried it.

33:40.040 --> 00:33:41.990
I don't like it.

33:42.040 --> 00:33:42.990
I said.

33:43.040 --> 00:33:44.990
What do you want to do then?

33:45.040 --> 00:33:45.990
That's Michael.

33:46.040 --> 00:33:47.990
Let's go to the social.

33:48.040 --> 00:33:48.990
Why?

33:49.040 --> 00:33:49.990
Michael asked.

33:50.040 --> 00:33:50.990
There's no one there now.

33:51.040 --> 00:33:52.990
So let's go.

33:53.040 --> 00:33:53.990
I said.

33:54.040 --> 00:33:54.990
And we went.

33:55.040 --> 00:33:58.990
Michael and I were in the boxing club.

33:59.040 --> 00:33:59.990
Okay.

34:00.040 --> 00:34:00.990
I said.

34:01.040 --> 00:34:02.990
You're the girl.

34:03.040 --> 00:34:05.990
Up and one and two.

34:06.040 --> 00:34:07.990
We did some of the moves together.

34:08.040 --> 00:34:09.990
It was good to dance again.

34:10.040 --> 00:34:11.990
Suddenly Michael stopped.

34:12.040 --> 00:34:12.990
What is it?

34:13.040 --> 00:34:14.990
I looked at the door.

34:15.040 --> 00:34:16.990
It was my dad.

34:17.040 --> 00:34:19.990
This time I didn't want to run.

34:20.040 --> 00:34:21.990
I didn't care.

34:22.040 --> 00:34:23.990
I walked over to him.

34:24.040 --> 00:34:25.990
I looked at him.

34:26.040 --> 00:34:28.990
And then I did my audition dance.

34:29.040 --> 00:34:30.990
I jumped and spun.

34:31.040 --> 00:34:33.990
I wanted to show dad everything.

34:34.040 --> 00:34:36.990
When I finished he didn't say anything.

34:37.040 --> 00:34:39.990
He looked at me and ran out of the room.

34:40.040 --> 00:34:41.990
Billy.

34:42.040 --> 00:34:43.990
What did you do that for?

34:44.040 --> 00:34:44.990
Said Michael.

34:45.040 --> 00:34:46.990
You're in big trouble now.

34:47.040 --> 00:34:48.990
He was right.

34:49.040 --> 00:34:52.990
But, well, that was Billy Elliot.

34:53.040 --> 00:34:54.990
Billy Elliot dances.

34:55.040 --> 34:57.040
That was me.

35:05.040 --> 00:35:06.990
Chapter 10.

35:07.040 --> 00:35:07.990
Jackie.

35:08.040 --> 00:35:09.990
The scab bus.

35:10.040 --> 00:35:12.990
I'm almost running down that road.

35:13.040 --> 00:35:13.990
Billy.

35:14.040 --> 00:35:15.990
Our Billy.

35:16.040 --> 00:35:17.990
He's good at something.

35:18.040 --> 00:35:18.990
No.

35:19.040 --> 00:35:19.990
Not good.

35:20.040 --> 00:35:20.990
Fantastic.

35:21.040 --> 00:35:23.990
Now, I don't know much about Bally.

35:24.040 --> 00:35:26.990
It's for posh people like that Mrs. Wilkinson.

35:27.040 --> 00:35:27.990
But maybe.

35:28.040 --> 00:35:29.990
Just maybe.

35:30.040 --> 00:35:31.990
My head spinning.

35:32.040 --> 00:35:34.990
And I'm thinking about my Sarah.

35:35.040 --> 00:35:35.990
My wife.

35:36.040 --> 00:35:38.990
I can almost hear her.

35:39.040 --> 00:35:40.990
Help the boy Jackie.

35:41.040 --> 00:35:41.990
What's wrong with you?

35:42.040 --> 00:35:43.990
He's our son.

35:44.040 --> 00:35:45.990
She's right.

35:46.040 --> 00:35:48.990
That Mrs. Wilkinson is right too.

35:49.040 --> 00:35:50.990
I'm going to see her.

35:51.040 --> 00:35:52.990
Now.

35:53.040 --> 00:35:55.990
Her husband opens the door.

35:56.040 --> 00:35:57.990
He looks at me.

35:58.040 --> 00:35:59.990
In there he says.

36:00.040 --> 00:36:01.990
I go into the living room.

36:02.040 --> 00:36:03.990
There she is with her cigarettes.

36:04.040 --> 00:36:06.990
How much has it gone to cost?

36:07.040 --> 00:36:07.990
I ask her.

36:08.040 --> 00:36:09.990
Happy Christmas to you too.

36:10.040 --> 00:36:10.990
She says.

36:11.040 --> 00:36:11.990
Then she smiles.

36:12.040 --> 00:36:13.990
Sit down.

36:14.040 --> 00:36:14.990
I'm okay.

36:15.040 --> 00:36:16.990
I don't want to stay for long.

36:17.040 --> 00:36:17.990
How much?

36:18.040 --> 00:36:19.990
For the audition.

36:20.040 --> 00:36:21.990
The cost of the bus to London.

36:22.040 --> 00:36:23.990
And a hotel for the night.

36:24.040 --> 00:36:25.990
I can help.

36:26.040 --> 00:36:27.990
I don't want your money.

36:28.040 --> 00:36:29.990
I say.

36:30.040 --> 00:36:31.990
How good is he?

36:32.040 --> 00:36:34.990
She smokes her cigarette and looks at me.

36:35.040 --> 00:36:37.990
He's the best Mr. Elliot.

36:38.040 --> 00:36:39.990
Thanks.

36:40.040 --> 00:36:40.990
I leave.

36:41.040 --> 00:36:42.990
I need time.

36:43.040 --> 00:36:44.990
I must think.

36:45.040 --> 00:36:46.990
What can I do?

36:47.040 --> 00:36:49.990
But I already know the answer.

36:50.040 --> 00:36:52.990
It's six o'clock in the morning.

36:53.040 --> 00:36:55.990
And I'm waiting for the bus with the other men.

36:56.040 --> 00:36:57.990
It's the scab bus.

36:58.040 --> 00:36:59.990
I'm doing it for Billy.

37:00.040 --> 00:37:01.990
I must help him.

37:02.040 --> 00:37:03.990
He's my son.

37:04.040 --> 00:37:05.990
I didn't sleep last night.

37:06.040 --> 00:37:07.990
I'm doing it for one week.

37:08.040 --> 00:37:11.990
One week's money for our Billy's audition.

37:12.040 --> 00:37:13.990
Our Tony doesn't know.

37:14.040 --> 00:37:15.990
No one knows yet.

37:16.040 --> 00:37:17.990
Only the other scabs.

37:18.040 --> 00:37:20.990
The bus comes and we all get on.

37:21.040 --> 00:37:23.990
No one speaks as we drive there.

37:24.040 --> 00:37:26.990
When we arrive, I can hear the men.

37:27.040 --> 00:37:29.990
Scab, scab, scab, they shout.

37:30.040 --> 00:37:31.990
I know the words.

37:32.040 --> 00:37:34.990
I shouted them last week.

37:35.040 --> 00:37:36.990
We drive through the men.

37:37.040 --> 00:37:38.990
Bang, bang, bang.

37:39.040 --> 00:37:40.990
They bang on the bus windows.

37:41.040 --> 00:37:42.990
The police try to stop them.

37:43.040 --> 00:37:44.990
The bus stops.

37:45.040 --> 00:37:47.990
Their faces are so close.

37:48.040 --> 00:37:49.990
I'm very frightened now.

37:50.040 --> 00:37:51.990
I look around me.

37:52.040 --> 00:37:54.990
Some of the scabs put their hands over their faces.

37:55.040 --> 00:37:55.990
Not me.

37:56.040 --> 00:37:57.990
I don't care.

37:58.040 --> 00:38:01.990
I look out of the window and then I see him.

38:02.040 --> 00:38:03.990
It's Tony.

38:04.040 --> 00:38:05.990
He's looking back at me.

38:06.040 --> 00:38:08.990
He can't believe his eyes.

38:09.040 --> 00:38:10.990
I don't know what to do.

38:11.040 --> 00:38:14.990
He can't believe his eyes.

38:15.040 --> 00:38:17.990
The bus moves on.

38:18.040 --> 00:38:19.990
Dad!

38:20.040 --> 00:38:21.990
Dad!

38:22.040 --> 00:38:23.990
What are you doing?

38:24.040 --> 00:38:25.990
I'm off the bus.

38:26.040 --> 00:38:27.990
I'm going to go into the mine.

38:28.040 --> 00:38:29.990
And there he is.

38:30.040 --> 00:38:31.990
Our Tony.

38:32.040 --> 00:38:33.990
He's calling to me.

38:34.040 --> 00:38:35.990
He's like a little boy again.

38:36.040 --> 00:38:37.990
I go over to him.

38:38.040 --> 00:38:39.990
I'm sorry, son.

38:40.040 --> 00:38:41.990
It's for Billy.

38:42.040 --> 00:38:42.990
I say.

38:43.040 --> 00:38:44.990
And then I start to cry.

38:45.040 --> 00:38:46.990
You can't go back, Dad.

38:47.040 --> 00:38:48.990
Not now.

38:49.040 --> 00:38:50.990
Tony looks at me.

38:51.040 --> 00:38:52.990
And he's crying too.

38:53.040 --> 00:38:54.990
There's another way, Dad.

38:55.040 --> 00:38:56.990
We can help Billy.

38:57.040 --> 38:59.040
Please.

39:01.040 --> 00:39:02.990
So I didn't go into the mine.

39:03.040 --> 00:39:04.990
I went home without Tony.

39:05.040 --> 00:39:07.990
I told him all about Billy in the ballet.

39:08.040 --> 00:39:10.990
We're going to find that money, Dad, he said.

39:11.040 --> 00:39:12.990
Billy's going to the audition.

39:13.040 --> 00:39:15.990
Tony had to be strong.

39:16.040 --> 00:39:17.990
I wasn't.

39:18.040 --> 39:20.040
Not now.

39:28.040 --> 00:39:29.990
Chapter 11.

39:30.040 --> 00:39:30.990
Billy.

39:31.040 --> 00:39:32.990
A stupid dream.

39:33.040 --> 00:39:36.990
I'm on a bus to London with me, Dad.

39:37.040 --> 00:39:38.990
I can't believe it.

39:39.040 --> 00:39:41.990
Wasn't it all a stupid dream?

39:42.040 --> 00:39:44.990
Me and the Royal Ballet School.

39:45.040 --> 00:39:47.990
But people in the town helped with the money.

39:48.040 --> 00:39:49.990
We had a dance at the social.

39:50.040 --> 00:39:53.990
And then there were some of my mom's things.

39:54.040 --> 00:39:57.990
I'm going to sell them, Dad said one morning.

39:58.040 --> 00:40:00.990
I don't want to think about that.

40:01.040 --> 00:40:04.990
I hated the Royal Ballet School when I saw it.

40:05.040 --> 00:40:07.990
It was so big and posh.

40:08.040 --> 00:40:10.990
How much is this going to cost, Dad said?

40:11.040 --> 00:40:13.990
I changed into my dance clothes.

40:14.040 --> 00:40:15.990
There were other boys there.

40:16.040 --> 00:40:17.990
They were posh too.

40:18.040 --> 00:40:19.990
They didn't understand my English.

40:20.040 --> 00:40:22.990
Sorry, what did you say?

40:23.040 --> 00:40:24.990
Oh, shut it.

40:25.040 --> 00:40:26.990
Then there was the audition.

40:27.040 --> 00:40:30.990
There were five people from the Royal Ballet School there.

40:31.040 --> 00:40:32.990
They sat behind a long table.

40:33.040 --> 00:40:34.990
They didn't like me.

40:35.040 --> 00:40:36.990
Do you have some music, Billy?

40:37.040 --> 00:40:38.990
I gave it to them.

40:39.040 --> 00:40:40.990
T-Rex.

40:41.040 --> 00:40:42.990
It wasn't right for that place.

40:43.040 --> 00:40:44.990
All that now.

40:45.040 --> 00:40:45.990
I didn't dance.

40:46.040 --> 00:40:47.990
I didn't move.

40:48.040 --> 00:40:49.990
I just looked at them.

40:50.040 --> 00:40:52.990
Then I heard Miss in my ear.

40:53.040 --> 00:40:55.990
Billy, you're not trying.

40:56.040 --> 00:40:56.990
Go on.

40:57.040 --> 00:40:58.990
Just do it.

40:59.040 --> 00:41:00.990
So I did it.

41:01.040 --> 00:41:02.990
Badly.

41:03.040 --> 00:41:05.990
When I finished, nobody said anything.

41:06.040 --> 00:41:08.990
They wrote some things down.

41:09.040 --> 00:41:10.990
Then one of them said,

41:11.040 --> 00:41:12.990
Thank you, Billy.

41:13.040 --> 00:41:14.990
You can go now.

41:15.040 --> 00:41:16.990
I almost ran out of there.

41:17.040 --> 00:41:18.990
All that work.

41:19.040 --> 00:41:19.990
All that money.

41:20.040 --> 00:41:20.990
For nothing.

41:21.040 --> 00:41:23.990
I just wanted to go home.

41:24.040 --> 00:41:26.990
But it wasn't over.

41:27.040 --> 00:41:29.990
They called me and Dad into the audition room again.

41:30.040 --> 00:41:32.990
We sat in front of that long table.

41:33.040 --> 00:41:35.990
Now, Billy, we have some questions for you.

41:36.040 --> 00:41:37.990
One of them said,

41:38.040 --> 00:41:39.990
Why do you like ballet?

41:40.040 --> 00:41:40.990
I didn't answer.

41:41.040 --> 00:41:42.990
I wasn't right for this place.

41:43.040 --> 00:41:44.990
Don't know, I said.

41:45.040 --> 00:41:47.990
Well, what do you like about dancing?

41:48.040 --> 00:41:49.990
Dad looked at me.

41:50.040 --> 00:41:52.990
Um, everything.

41:53.040 --> 00:41:55.990
He dances all the time, my Dad said.

41:56.040 --> 00:41:59.990
Yes, we've got a letter from Mrs Wilkinson here.

42:00.040 --> 00:42:00.990
I knew Mr Elliot.

42:01.040 --> 00:42:02.990
Did you like ballet?

42:03.040 --> 00:42:06.990
Um, well, I don't know much about it, Dad said.

42:07.040 --> 00:42:08.990
Well, that was true.

42:09.040 --> 00:42:10.990
And that was about it.

42:11.040 --> 00:42:12.990
We got up and walked to the door.

42:13.040 --> 00:42:14.990
One more thing, Billy.

42:15.040 --> 00:42:17.990
Said a very posh woman.

42:18.040 --> 00:42:21.990
How do you feel when you dance?

42:22.040 --> 00:42:23.990
I thought for a minute.

42:24.040 --> 00:42:25.990
I feel good.

42:26.040 --> 00:42:27.990
I started.

42:28.040 --> 00:42:30.990
When I dance, I forget the world.

42:31.040 --> 00:42:32.990
And the strike.

42:33.040 --> 00:42:34.990
And everything.

42:35.040 --> 00:42:37.990
There's fire in my body.

42:38.040 --> 00:42:39.990
It's like...

42:40.040 --> 00:42:42.990
It's like flying.

42:43.040 --> 42:46.040
That sounded stupid, I thought.

42:55.040 --> 00:42:55.990
Chapter 12.

42:56.040 --> 00:42:57.990
Jackie.

42:58.040 --> 00:42:59.990
The letter.

43:00.040 --> 00:43:01.990
Poor Billy.

43:02.040 --> 00:43:04.990
When we got home, he went to bed.

43:05.040 --> 00:43:06.990
He didn't want any dinner.

43:07.040 --> 00:43:08.990
He didn't want to talk.

43:09.040 --> 00:43:10.990
And that place.

43:11.040 --> 00:43:13.990
It was a different world.

43:14.040 --> 00:43:15.990
All those rich boys.

43:16.040 --> 00:43:17.990
Special dancing lessons.

43:18.040 --> 00:43:18.990
Big houses.

43:19.040 --> 00:43:20.990
Posh cars.

43:21.040 --> 00:43:22.990
It wasn't off.

43:23.040 --> 00:43:26.990
But the royal ballet people.

43:27.040 --> 00:43:29.990
Maybe they weren't so bad.

43:30.040 --> 00:43:33.990
When we left the audition room, one of the teachers said,

43:34.040 --> 00:43:37.990
Good luck with the strike, Mr. Elliot.

43:38.040 --> 00:43:39.990
We waited one week.

43:40.040 --> 00:43:41.990
Two weeks.

43:42.040 --> 00:43:44.990
Then the letter arrived.

43:45.040 --> 00:43:46.990
Billy was at school.

43:47.040 --> 00:43:48.990
It was a long day.

43:49.040 --> 00:43:50.990
Billy came home at four o'clock.

43:51.040 --> 00:43:53.990
We were all there.

43:54.040 --> 00:43:56.990
Billy took the letter.

43:57.040 --> 00:43:58.990
No one said anything.

43:59.040 --> 00:44:02.990
He went into his nuns' room and closed the door.

44:03.040 --> 00:44:04.990
Then.

44:05.040 --> 00:44:06.990
Nothing.

44:07.040 --> 00:44:08.990
He didn't come out.

44:09.040 --> 00:44:11.990
In the end, we went in there.

44:12.040 --> 00:44:13.990
I opened the door.

44:14.040 --> 00:44:17.990
Billy started to cry.

44:18.040 --> 00:44:18.990
I did it.

44:19.040 --> 00:44:20.990
He said quietly.

44:21.040 --> 44:23.040
I'm in.

44:25.040 --> 00:44:26.990
Yes!

44:27.040 --> 00:44:28.990
I ran up the road to the social.

44:29.040 --> 00:44:29.990
He did it.

44:30.040 --> 00:44:31.990
Our Billy.

44:32.040 --> 00:44:33.990
I wanted to tell everyone.

44:34.040 --> 00:44:35.990
I ran into the social.

44:36.040 --> 00:44:36.990
He's in.

44:37.040 --> 00:44:37.990
He did it.

44:38.040 --> 00:44:39.990
Nobody answered.

44:40.040 --> 00:44:41.990
It's over, Jackie.

44:42.040 --> 00:44:43.990
We're going back.

44:44.040 --> 00:44:45.990
What?

44:46.040 --> 00:44:47.990
The strike's over.

44:48.040 --> 00:44:51.990
We're going back to work on Monday.

44:52.040 --> 00:44:53.990
So that was it.

44:54.040 --> 00:44:57.990
The mind didn't stay open very long after that.

44:58.040 --> 00:44:59.990
That was ten years ago now.

45:00.040 --> 00:45:02.990
It was the end for me.

45:03.040 --> 00:45:06.990
But life is only just starting for Billy.

45:07.040 --> 45:09.040
And that's something.

45:17.040 --> 00:45:18.990
Epilogue.

45:19.040 --> 00:45:19.990
Jackie.

45:20.040 --> 00:45:21.990
Our Billy.

45:22.040 --> 00:45:24.990
Well, London doesn't change.

45:25.040 --> 00:45:26.990
It's still big.

45:27.040 --> 00:45:28.990
It's still expensive.

45:29.040 --> 00:45:30.990
But we didn't pay for our ballet tickets.

45:31.040 --> 00:45:32.990
I'm sitting here without Tony.

45:33.040 --> 00:45:36.990
It's funny to see your name in big letters.

45:37.040 --> 00:45:37.990
There.

45:38.040 --> 00:45:40.990
On the front of the Royal Opera House.

45:41.040 --> 00:45:42.990
The Royal Ballet.

45:43.040 --> 00:45:44.990
Billy Elliot.

45:45.040 --> 00:45:46.990
Our Billy.

45:47.040 --> 00:45:49.990
Then the music starts.

45:50.040 --> 00:45:51.990
And there he is.

45:52.040 --> 00:45:54.990
He runs on and jumps.

45:55.040 --> 00:45:55.990
What a jump!

45:56.040 --> 00:45:57.990
No one does it like Billy.

45:58.040 --> 00:45:59.990
He spins and spins.

46:00.040 --> 00:46:01.990
Everyone's watching.

46:02.040 --> 00:46:03.990
He's the best.

46:04.040 --> 00:46:04.990
And he's smiling all the time.

46:05.040 --> 00:46:06.990
He's smiling at us.

46:07.040 --> 00:46:08.990
So I stand up and I shout,

46:09.040 --> 00:46:10.990
Billy, Billy Elliot.

46:11.040 --> 00:46:12.990
Tony's standing with me.

46:13.040 --> 00:46:14.990
Our Billy, his shouts.

46:15.040 --> 00:46:16.990
And other people stand up too.

46:17.040 --> 00:46:18.990
And you know,

46:19.040 --> 00:46:20.990
I'm never going to forget this.

46:21.040 --> 46:24.040
It's the best time of my life.

46:26.040 --> 46:31.040
MUSIC
